# Shell scripts must stay LF: a CRLF checkout breaks the shebang under WSL
# ("env: bash\r: No such file or directory") and \r leaks into every parsed
# string under Git Bash. Windows clones default to core.autocrlf=true, so
# without this file the tool is broken on Windows out of the box.
* text=auto
bin/husk text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
